    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass. \n\nI implemented the change with minimal structural impact:\n\n1. **New helper `MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 a small, cohesive class (one static method, no surrounding complexity) following the existing pattern of `AgeBand`, `CheckDigit`, etc. It computes: base 1 + email + no-namesake, capped at 3 (the pre-tenure factors), then `+1` only when tenure (`registrationDate` \u2192 today) exceeds 365 days, reaching level 4.\n\n2. **One edited line in `OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the `membershipLevel` expression now delegates to `MembershipLevel.of(owner)` instead of inlining the formula.\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is today (zero tenure), it can never exceed level 3 \u2014 a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount` 0 lands exactly at 3, as required and as verified by `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3`. Level 4 is reserved for owners whose tenure passes 365 days.",
